ckgroundColor=#ffffff;fontFamily=Segoe UI;entryX=0;entryY=0.12;entryPerimeter=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c28" target="c19"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="52" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=1;strokeColor=#334155;edgeStyle=none;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;fontFamily=Segoe UI;entryX=1;entryY=0.15;entryPerimeter=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c31" target="c4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="53" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=1;strokeColor=#334155;edgeStyle=none;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;fontFamily=Segoe UI;entryX=1;entryY=0.85;entryPerimeter=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c32" target="c7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="54" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=1;strokeColor=#334155;edgeStyle=none;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;fontFamily=Segoe UI;entryX=1;entryY=0.12;entryPerimeter=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c32" target="c12"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="55" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=1;strokeColor=#334155;edgeStyle=none;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;fontFamily=Segoe UI;entryX=1;entryY=0.2;entryPerimeter=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c32" target="c15"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="56" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=1;strokeColor=#334155;edgeStyle=none;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;fontFamily=Segoe UI;entryX=1;entryY=0.82;entryPerimeter=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c33" target="c15"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="57" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=1;strokeColor=#334155;edgeStyle=none;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;fontFamily=Segoe UI;dashed=1;strokeColor=#64748b;fontColor=#64748b;entryX=1;entryY=0.82;entryPerimeter=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c34" target="c19"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="58" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt; — Level 0 as in Figure 2.1: a line joins an actor to a subsystem it uses; each package shows 2–4 representative use cases of its range (55 codes in all, 50 in use; the full lists are in Figures 2.1–2.6). The Investor inherits the Customer use cases (generalization, hollow triangle at Customer) {not the Batch's Operator or its related parties}. UC10, UC27 and UC30 include UC12 Make Payment (only UC10 → UC12 drawn); UC40 Monitor Payout Reconciliation is a separate Administrator use case in SD5. UC54 Forfeit Deposit «extend» UC55 Cancel Bulk Pre-order {the Batch opened} and «extend» UC30 {the Customer refuses delivery or does not pay the balance}; in the UC30 case UC50 Record Invoiced Sale resells the crabs. UC21 View Production Timeline (SD3) is used by the Operator, the Investor and the Administrator. Background jobs are system behaviour, not actors. Dashed grey or «planned» = in Register v1.4, not on develop yet; &quot;(… «planned»)&quot; = the v1.4 part of an existing use case. Removed in v1.4, codes not reused: UC13, UC23, UC24, UC26, UC46.&lt;br&gt;Design decisions of 05/11/2026 applied here were confirmed by the lead." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#94a3b8;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=10;fontFamily=Segoe UI;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1106" width="1574" height="87" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram name="O3 Conceptual ERD" id="O3_Conceptual_ERD"><mxGraphModel dx="1200" dy="800" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1654" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="2" value="&lt;b&gt;Figure O.3 – Conceptual ERD: 20 core business entities of Register v1.4, no attributes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot; color=&quot;#64748b&quot;&gt;v3.2 · 05/11/2026 · Register v1.4&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAl